        {
          "path": "packages/core/src/errors/error-reporter.ts",
          "startLine": 88,
          "endLine": 92,
          "side": "right",
          "category": "Code Defect",
          "origin": "ai",
          "text": "The value of `SIX_WEEKS_IN_MS` (approx 42 days) exceeds the maximum delay supported by `setTimeout` in Node.js (approx 24.8 days, or 2^31-1 ms). \n\nFor fresh releases, `releaseExpiresInMs` will exceed this limit, causing the timeout to trigger immediately (or with a very short delay), effectively disabling error tracking right after startup.\n\n**Suggestion:**\nInstead of using `setTimeout`, store the expiration timestamp in a class property (e.g., `this.releaseExpirationTime`) and check `if (Date.now() > this.releaseExpirationTime)` inside the `beforeSend` method.\n"
        }
      ]
    },
